<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan's CPC buys August naphtha at $193/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan's CPC buys August naphtha at $193/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has awarded its tender to buy August naphthenic and aromatic naphtha (N+A) at $193 per tonne, a company official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>CPC purchased the 28,000-tonne cargo for August 1-10 delivery on a cost and freight basis to Kaohsiung.</p>
<p>The company official said CPC will decide by Friday if it is to award a second cargo for delivery in the second half of August.</p>
<p>The tender closed June 25 and was valid for two days.  </p>
<p>CPC's last tender, for July 20-31 delivery was awarded at slightly above $215 per tonne c+f Kaohsiung.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3082)</p>
